{
  "title": "Diagram block test: boxes, boundaries, arrows",
  "content": {
    "summary": "The diagram block draws boxes, boundaries, and arrows the browser lays out, and walks them one step per Next.",
    "meta": "2026-10-07 · present test page · diagram block",
    "chips": [
      {
        "text": "3 diagrams",
        "style": "stat"
      },
      {
        "text": "2 group levels",
        "style": "stat"
      },
      {
        "text": "9 steps",
        "style": "stat"
      }
    ],
    "sections": [
      {
        "h": "What this page tests",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "t": "p",
            "text": "Every piece of the diagram block is on this page once, in the brief and again on a slide."
          },
          {
            "t": "list",
            "items": [
              "Three diagrams: a context view, a cluster with two levels of groups, and a top to bottom pipeline.",
              "Five node kinds: service, store, queue, person, external.",
              "Stepped walkthroughs with focus on one box and on a whole group.",
              "Charts without a card, one with frame set to true, and an image without its border."
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "h": "System context",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "t": "p",
            "text": "Two people, two hosted systems, and the platform between them. **Flow edges** carry dots whose speed follows their weight, so the shopper's traffic runs faster than the support agent's."
          },
          {
            "t": "diagram",
            "caption": "Who talks to the platform and what sits beside it. Purple is people, green the platform's own services, grey the systems outside it; the amber boundary is the platform.",
            "direction": "LR",
            "groups": [
              {
                "id": "platform",
                "label": "the platform",
                "tone": "amber"
              }
            ],
            "nodes": [
              {
                "id": "shopper",
                "label": "Shopper",
                "text": "a browser on a phone",
                "kind": "person",
                "tone": "purple"
              },
              {
                "id": "support",
                "label": "Support agent",
                "text": "the back office app",
                "kind": "person",
                "tone": "purple"
              },
              {
                "id": "gateway",
                "label": "Gateway",
                "text": "Envoy, TLS and routing",
                "group": "platform",
                "tone": "green"
              },
              {
                "id": "checkout",
                "label": "Checkout",
                "text": "orders, pricing, stock",
                "group": "platform",
                "tone": "green"
              },
              {
                "id": "psp",
                "label": "Payment provider",
                "text": "cards and wallets, hosted",
                "kind": "external",
                "tone": "neutral"
              },
              {
                "id": "mail",
                "label": "Mail service",
                "text": "receipts, hosted",
                "kind": "external",
                "tone": "neutral"
              }
            ],
            "edges": [
              {
                "from": "shopper",
                "to": "gateway",
                "label": "buys",
                "flow": true,
                "weight": 200
              },
              {
                "from": "support",
                "to": "gateway",
                "label": "refunds",
                "flow": true,
                "weight": 20
              },
              {
                "from": "gateway",
                "to": "checkout",
                "label": "routes",
                "flow": true,
                "weight": 220
              },
              {
                "from": "checkout",
                "to": "psp",
                "label": "charges"
              },
              {
                "from": "psp",
                "to": "checkout",
                "label": "webhooks"
              },
              {
                "from": "checkout",
                "to": "mail",
                "label": "sends receipts"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "h": "Inside the prod cluster, two levels of groups",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "t": "p",
            "text": "The cluster holds two namespaces. Boxes in a chain inside a group now sit the **same layer gap apart** as boxes at the root, so the labels on the runs between them stay clear of the boxes."
          },
          {
            "t": "diagram",
            "caption": "An order inside the prod cluster, namespace by namespace. Green boxes are the cluster's own services, blue its stores and queues, grey the edge; the amber boundary is the data namespace.",
            "direction": "LR",
            "groups": [
              {
                "id": "prod",
                "label": "prod cluster"
              },
              {
                "id": "ns_checkout",
                "label": "checkout namespace",
                "group": "prod",
                "step": 1
              },
              {
                "id": "ns_data",
                "label": "data namespace",
                "tone": "amber",
                "group": "prod",
                "step": 4
              }
            ],
            "nodes": [
              {
                "id": "gw",
                "label": "Gateway",
                "text": "Envoy, terminates TLS",
                "group": "prod",
                "tone": "neutral"
              },
              {
                "id": "api",
                "label": "Checkout API",
                "text": "Go, validates the cart",
                "group": "ns_checkout",
                "step": 1,
                "tone": "green"
              },
              {
                "id": "pricing",
                "label": "Pricing",
                "text": "Go, quotes and discounts",
                "group": "ns_checkout",
                "step": 2,
                "tone": "green"
              },
              {
                "id": "stock",
                "label": "Stock",
                "text": "Go, reserves units",
                "group": "ns_checkout",
                "step": 3,
                "tone": "green"
              },
              {
                "id": "orders",
                "label": "Orders DB",
                "text": "Postgres, one row per order",
                "kind": "store",
                "group": "ns_data",
                "step": 4,
                "tone": "blue"
              },
              {
                "id": "events",
                "label": "Order events",
                "text": "Kafka, one topic",
                "kind": "queue",
                "group": "ns_data",
                "step": 4,
                "tone": "blue"
              },
              {
                "id": "mailer",
                "label": "Mailer",
                "text": "sends the receipt",
                "group": "ns_checkout",
                "step": 5,
                "tone": "green"
              }
            ],
            "edges": [
              {
                "from": "gw",
                "to": "api",
                "label": "route",
                "flow": true,
                "weight": 300,
                "step": 1
              },
              {
                "from": "api",
                "to": "pricing",
                "label": "quote",
                "step": 2
              },
              {
                "from": "pricing",
                "to": "api",
                "label": "price",
                "step": 2
              },
              {
                "from": "api",
                "to": "stock",
                "label": "reserve",
                "step": 3
              },
              {
                "from": "api",
                "to": "orders",
                "label": "insert",
                "step": 4
              },
              {
                "from": "api",
                "to": "events",
                "label": "order placed",
                "flow": true,
                "weight": 300,
                "step": 4
              },
              {
                "from": "events",
                "to": "mailer",
                "label": "consume",
                "flow": true,
                "weight": 300,
                "step": 5
              }
            ],
            "steps": [
              {
                "caption": "The gateway routes the request into the checkout namespace.",
                "focus": [
                  "api"
                ]
              },
              {
                "caption": "The API asks pricing for a quote and gets the price back.",
                "focus": [
                  "pricing"
                ]
              },
              {
                "caption": "Stock reserves the units.",
                "focus": [
                  "stock"
                ]
              },
              {
                "caption": "The order is written and an event goes on the topic.",
                "focus": [
                  "ns_data"
                ]
              },
              {
                "caption": "The mailer consumes the event and sends the receipt."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "t": "p",
            "text": "Step four focuses the whole data namespace: the group, everything inside it, and the edges that touch its boxes light up. The last step has no focus, so the finished picture shows plain."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "h": "Top to bottom, the release pipeline",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "t": "p",
            "text": "The same block with direction set to TB. The layers run down the page and the edge labels sit beside the vertical runs, so the layer gap stays at its default."
          },
          {
            "t": "diagram",
            "caption": "From a pull request to a running service, top to bottom. Blue is GitHub, green the fleet, purple the developer.",
            "direction": "TB",
            "groups": [
              {
                "id": "gh",
                "label": "GitHub",
                "step": 1
              },
              {
                "id": "fleet",
